course: dictionary
lesson: 460
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Grandpa dozed in his armchair.» Here an armchair is a comfortable chair with side parts to rest your arms on. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is being described? A chair, a room, a place?
explain: «One afternoon, while the Rat dozes in his armchair hunting for rhymes, the Mole quietly decides to go out by himself.» The Rat is sitting still and relaxing, so armchair means the comfy chair, not a sport or a hobby.
explain: The second meaning is used in a different way. It is informal, and it comes before a noun: an armchair fan is someone who follows a team and cheers from the sofa, not someone who plays. Clues like "only watches" or "never does" help you spot it.
fact: An armchair is a comfortable chair with side parts to rest your arms on.
fact: Informal: an armchair fan, an armchair traveller and an armchair expert are people who follow or talk about something without doing it themselves.
fact: Armchair can also be an adjective, and it always comes before a noun.
fact: The plural of armchair is armchairs.
fact: Context tells you which meaning a word has.
exercise: «Grandpa dozed in his armchair.» What is an armchair in this sentence? | A soft bed for sleeping outside | *A comfortable chair with side parts to rest your arms on | A small table by the window
exercise: Maya says she is an armchair expert on football, but she has never played. What does armchair mean here? | *Someone who talks about it without doing it themselves | Someone who is very good at playing it | Someone who sits in a chair all day | A kind of football boot
exercise: Find the plural of armchair in this list. | sofa | cushion | rest | *armchairs
test: «The Rat dozes in his armchair hunting for rhymes.» Which word tells you the Rat is relaxed? | *dozes | rhymes | decides | hunting
test: In «an armchair traveller», what does armchair suggest? | Someone who travels by train every day | A comfy seat on a bus | *Someone who reads about trips but never goes | Someone who is always lost
exam: Which sentence uses armchair in the informal sense? | *«Dad is an armchair expert on cooking, but he never cooks.» | «Grandma reads in her armchair by the window.» | «The armchairs were covered in dust.»
